# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this file for "Cite this repository", and
# Zenodo reads .zenodo.json (which takes precedence there) when a release is archived.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Fiscal Policy Calculator or its figures, please cite it as below.
  For a single figure, cite the page's own "Cite as" line, which carries the
  scores date, and give the snapshot id from https://fiscal.lwilsesamson.com/data.
type: software
title: Fiscal Policy Calculator
abstract: >-
  Ten-year budget estimates for U.S. tax and spending proposals, each shown
  beside the published score (CBO, JCT, Treasury and others) it is checked
  against, with out-of-sample error reported by policy class. Includes the
  Python scoring engine, the nightly static export the website reads, and
  frozen snapshots of every set of scored figures the site has published.
authors:
  - family-names: Wilse-Samson
    given-names: Laurence
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/laurencehw/fiscal-policy-calculator
url: https://fiscal.lwilsesamson.com
keywords:
  - fiscal policy
  - budget scoring
  - tax policy
  - public finance
  - microsimulation
  - CBO
